
---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Profile｜Nishikino Official Website"
  description="Meet Nishikino, a creator inspired by Japanese traditions, architecture, and the beauty of everyday discoveries. Through Minecraft and video, I bring the things I love to life."
>

<section id="profileSection" class="relative min-h-screen overflow-hidden">

  <!-- Background -->
  <img
    id="profileBg1"
    src="/images/profile-bg.webp"
    alt="Profile background"
    class="profile-bg profile-bg-front absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover select-none pointer-events-none"
    draggable="false"
  />

  <img
    id="profileBg2"
    src="/images/profile-bg-message.webp"
    alt=""
    class="profile-bg profile-bg-back absolute inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover select-none pointer-events-none"
    draggable="false"
  />

  <!-- Content -->
  <div
    class="relative z-10 mx-auto flex min-h-screen max-w-[1700px]
           flex-col items-center justify-between
           px-5 py-24
           sm:px-8 sm:py-28
           lg:flex-row lg:px-20 lg:py-24"
  >

    <!-- Left -->
    <div
      id="profileLeft"
      class="profile-content w-full lg:w-[30%]"
    >

      <p
        class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.35em] text-white
               sm:text-sm sm:tracking-[0.55em]"
        style="font-family:'Inter',sans-serif;"
      >
        PROFILE
      </p>

      <h1
        class="mt-4 text-3xl font-light text-white
               sm:text-5xl
               lg:mt-6 lg:text-6xl"
        style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
      >
        NISHIKINO
      </h1>

      <p
        class="mt-6 text-xs leading-6 text-white
               sm:text-base sm:leading-10
               lg:mt-8"
        style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
      >
        Nishikino
        <br />
        A creator inspired by Japanese traditions and architecture,
        <br />
        bringing captivating worlds to life through Minecraft and video ✧*˙˚
        <br /><br />

        I love exploring famous places,
        <br />
        capturing landscapes and moments on camera,
        <br />
        and following my curiosity wherever it takes me.
        <br />
        I turn the things I love into creations of my own!
      </p>

    </div>

    <!-- Center -->
    <div class="hidden lg:block lg:w-[18%]"></div>

    <!-- Right -->
    <div
      class="profile-content delay mt-10 w-full space-y-5
             sm:mt-12 sm:space-y-6
             lg:mt-0 lg:w-[34%] lg:space-y-6"
    >

      <!-- INTRODUCTION -->
      <div
        id="introductionCard"
        class="profile-card rounded-[24px] border border-white/20
               p-5 sm:rounded-[34px] sm:p-8"
      >

        <p
          class="text-[9px] tracking-[0.35em] text-white/60
                 sm:text-xs sm:tracking-[0.45em]"
        >
          INTRODUCTION
        </p>

        <div
          class="mt-4 space-y-3 text-xs leading-6 text-white
                 sm:mt-5 sm:space-y-4 sm:text-base sm:leading-8"
          style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
        >

          <p>
            The first character in my name, <strong>錦 (Nishiki)</strong>,
            evokes the colorful beauty and richness of brocade.
            The second, <strong>乃 (No)</strong>,
            has an elegant, classical feel.
            <br />
            I brought these two characters together with the wish
            to express something rich and beautiful.
            That's how my name came to be!
          </p>

          <div class="border-t border-white/15 pt-4 text-white/90">
            <p>Yua Tousaka (東坂 優亜)</p>
            <p>Birthday: May 4, 2003</p>
            <p>Birthplace: Ota, Gunma, Japan</p>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- MESSAGE -->
      <div
        id="messageCard"
        class="profile-card rounded-[24px] border border-white/20
               p-5 sm:rounded-[34px] sm:p-8"
      >

        <p
          class="text-[10px] tracking-[0.4em] text-white/60
                 sm:text-xs sm:tracking-[0.45em]"
        >
          MESSAGE
        </p>

        <div
          class="mt-5 text-[13px] leading-7 text-white/100
                 sm:text-base sm:leading-8"
          style="font-family:'Shippori Mincho',serif;"
        >

          <p>
            I've been fascinated by Japanese architecture since the early days of Minecraft 1.1.<br />
            I bring moments that look almost like real photographs to life in Minecraft.
          </p>

          <p class="mt-4">
            Through Minecraft, one of the world's most popular sandbox games,
            I recreate Japan's historic landmarks and traditional townscapes,
            as well as create landscapes and worlds that don't exist in reality.<br />
            I'm a creator who wants to share the joy of turning the things I love into works of art,
            along with the beauty of Japanese history and traditions.
            ✧*˙˚
          </p>

          <details id="messageDetails" class="mt-6 group">

            <!-- Read More -->
            <summary
              id="messageSummary"
              class="cursor-pointer select-none text-rose-200 transition hover:text-white/100"
            >
              ▶ Read More
            </summary>

            <!-- MESSAGE DETAIL -->
            <div
              class="mt-6 space-y-6 text-[13px] leading-7 text-white/100
                     sm:text-base sm:leading-8"
            >

              <p>
                I've loved cityscapes and the energy of bustling streets ever since I was little.<br />
                When you're walking through a town, do you ever find yourself noticing
                the shapes of buildings, the streets, little shops, or the scenery around you?<br />
                I'm often drawn to something quietly standing out in the middle of a busy city.
                My interest in Japanese traditions and architecture grew from those small moments of fascination.
              </p>

              <p>
                Japanese castles and traditional architecture have a special place in my heart, too.<br />
                Magnificent keeps, beautiful rooftops, intricate decorations, and enormous stone walls...<br />
                I find them absolutely breathtaking.<br />
                When I was in middle school, I happened to see the keep of Edo Castle
                depicted in the historical folding screen known as the
                <em>Edo-zu Byōbu</em>.<br />
                I fell in love with it at first sight.<br />
                That was where everything began.
              </p>

              <p>
                My journey into Minecraft building actually started with a simple idea.
                In Survival Mode, I was determined to build a house
                that enemies wouldn't be able to destroy.<br />
                That determination led me to build a castle keep,
                which became the starting point of my architectural creations.
              </p>

              <p>
                A few months later, I began thinking,
                "Wouldn't it be wonderful if I could look at the places I love whenever I wanted?"<br />
                I wanted to recreate real landmarks, buildings, and castles
                in places of my own choosing.<br />
                And it didn't stop there.
                I also started bringing back buildings that no longer exist
                and creating entire worlds from my imagination.
              </p>

              <p>
                As a result, I began exploring cities,
                visiting famous landmarks and Japanese castles,
                as well as places connected to the Tokugawa family.<br />
                I started sharing the things I love through my own creations,
                in my own way!
              </p>

              <p>
                At first, I simply enjoyed all of this as a hobby.<br />
                But as more and more people began appreciating my work,
                I gradually started receiving offers for commissioned projects and collaborations...
              </p>

              <p>
                There's a Japanese saying that dates back to the Edo period:
                <em>"Suki koso mono no jōzu nare."</em><br />
                It roughly means, "Passion is the key to mastery."<br />
                As I go about my everyday life, I often find myself thinking
                just how true those words really are.
              </p>

              <p>
                My architectural style is rooted in the Japanese architecture I love,
                with faithful recreations of real buildings at its heart ✧*˙˚.
              </p>

              <p>
                I absolutely adore Japanese architecture.
                It's beautiful, impressive, and full of charm...<br />
                But I have plenty of other interests, too!<br />

                I enjoy playing all kinds of Steam games,
                going out to take photographs, and listening to music.<br />
                I'm especially fond of upbeat pop songs♪<br />

                I also watch a lot of anime!
                I tend to enjoy stories with serious developments
                and worlds that really draw me in.<br />
                <em>My Hero Academia</em> and
                <em>Toilet-Bound Hanako-kun</em> are two of my particular favorites ✧*˙˚<br />

                I love traveling and sightseeing, too.
                Looking around different cityscapes
                and exploring places I've never visited before
                are some of my favorite things to do.

                I also enjoy cute things, delicious coffee,
                fashion, and beauty.<br />
                I'm a big fan of YouTubers and voice actors as well,
                and I often watch videos and works featuring people who catch my interest!
              </p>

              <p>
                I believe there are still so many interesting things
                waiting to be discovered in our everyday lives!<br />
                I enjoy finding those little discoveries,
                doing what I love, and making the most of every moment.
                ✧*˙˚
              </p>

            </div>

            <div class="message-actions">

              <button
                id="collapseMessage"
                type="button"
                class="cursor-pointer select-none text-rose-200 transition hover:text-white"
              >
              </button>

            </div>

          </details>

        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

</section>


<style>

/* ========================================
   Background
======================================== */

.profile-bg {
  animation: profileFloat 12s ease-in-out infinite;
  transition: opacity .7s ease;
}

.profile-bg-front {
  opacity: 1;
}

.profile-bg-back {
  opacity: 0;
}

@keyframes profileFloat {
  0% {
    transform: scale(1.05) translateY(0px);
  }
  50% {
    transform: scale(1.08) translateY(-15px);
  }
  100% {
    transform: scale(1.05) translateY(0px);
  }
}


/* ========================================
   Content Animation
======================================== */

.profile-content {
  opacity: 0;
  transform: translateY(80px) scale(.96);
  animation: profileAppear 1.2s cubic-bezier(.18,.89,.32,1.28) forwards;
}

.profile-content.delay {
  animation-delay: .25s;
}

@keyframes profileAppear {
  0% {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(80px) scale(.96);
  }
  70% {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(-12px) scale(1.02);
  }
  100% {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0) scale(1);
  }
}


/* ========================================
   Glass Cards
======================================== */

.profile-card {
  position: relative;

  /* Frosted glass effect */
  background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.20) !important;
  backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(14px);

  border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2) !important;

  transition: transform .6s ease, background .6s ease;
  animation: cardFloat 8s ease-in-out infinite;

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}

.profile-card:nth-child(2) {
  animation-delay: 1s;
}

@keyframes cardFloat {
  0% {
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
  50% {
    transform: translateY(-8px);
  }
  100% {
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
}


/* ========================================
   Details
======================================== */

details summary {
  list-style: none;
}

details summary::-webkit-details-marker {
  display: none;
}


/* ========================================
   Browser Color Settings
======================================== */

:global(html) {
  color-scheme: light;
}

:global(body) {
  color-scheme: light;
  -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
}


/* ========================================
   Text Colors
======================================== */

.profile-content p,
.profile-content h1,
.profile-content h2,
.profile-content h3,
.profile-content strong {
  forced-color-adjust: none;
}


/* PROFILE label */

.profile-content > p:first-child {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
}


/* PROFILE name */

.profile-content h1 {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
}


/* Profile introduction text */

.profile-content > p:not(:first-child) {
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
}


/* ========================================
   Card Text
======================================== */

.profile-card > p:first-child {
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}

.profile-card > div {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}

.profile-card > div p {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}

.profile-card > div > div.border-t {
  border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15) !important;

  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}

.profile-card > div > div.border-t p {
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
}


/* ========================================
   Message Details
======================================== */

#messageDetails {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  forced-color-adjust: none;
}

#messageDetails > div {
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}

#messageDetails > div p {
  color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
}


/* Read More */

#messageSummary {
  color: rgb(254, 205, 211) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgb(254, 205, 211);

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}

#messageSummary:hover {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
}


/* Links */

#messageDetails a {
  color: rgb(254, 205, 211) !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: rgb(254, 205, 211);

  forced-color-adjust: none;
}

#messageDetails a:hover {
  color: #ffffff !important;
  -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
}


/* ========================================
   Smartphone
======================================== */

@media (max-width: 639px) {

  .profile-content,
  .profile-content *,
  .profile-card,
  .profile-card *,
  #messageDetails,
  #messageDetails *,
  #messageSummary {
    forced-color-adjust: none;
  }

  /* Preserve glass effect on smartphones */

  .profile-card {
    background: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.20) !important;
    backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
    -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(14px);

    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2) !important;
  }

  .profile-content > p:first-child,
  .profile-content h1 {
    color: #ffffff !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
  }

  .profile-content > p:not(:first-child) {
    font-size: 14px !important;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
  }

  .profile-card > p:first-child {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6) !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.6);
  }

  .profile-card > div,
  .profile-card > div p {
    font-size: 14px !important;
    color: #ffffff !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: #ffffff;
  }

  .profile-card > div > div.border-t,
  .profile-card > div > div.border-t p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);

    border-top-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.15) !important;
  }

  #messageDetails > div,
  #messageDetails > div p {
    font-size: 14px !important;
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9) !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
  }

  #messageSummary,
  #messageDetails a {
    color: rgb(254, 205, 211) !important;
    -webkit-text-fill-color: rgb(254, 205, 211);
  }


  /* Layout adjustment when MESSAGE is expanded */

  #profileSection.message-open #profileLeft,
  #profileSection.message-open #introductionCard {
    display: none !important;
  }

  #profileSection.message-open > div.relative.z-10 {
    justify-content: flex-start !important;
  }

  #profileSection.message-open #messageCard {
    width: 100% !important;
  }

}


/* ========================================
   Smartphone Background
======================================== */

@media (max-width: 639px) {

  #profileBg2 {
    object-position: center center !important;
  }

}

</style>


<script is:inline>
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", () => {

  const section = document.getElementById("profileSection");
  const profileLeft = document.getElementById("profileLeft");
  const introductionCard = document.getElementById("introductionCard");
  const messageCard = document.getElementById("messageCard");

  const details = document.getElementById("messageDetails");
  const summary = document.getElementById("messageSummary");

  const bg1 = document.getElementById("profileBg1");
  const bg2 = document.getElementById("profileBg2");

  if (
    !section ||
    !profileLeft ||
    !introductionCard ||
    !messageCard ||
    !details ||
    !summary ||
    !bg1 ||
    !bg2
  ) return;


  details.addEventListener("toggle", () => {

    const isMobile = window.innerWidth <= 639;

    if (details.open) {

      /* Switch background */

      bg1.style.opacity = "0";
      bg2.style.opacity = "1";

      /* Collapse button text */

      summary.textContent = "  ▶ Collapse";


      if (isMobile) {

        profileLeft.style.display = "none";
        introductionCard.style.display = "none";

        /* Make MESSAGE full width */

        messageCard.style.width = "100%";

        /* Position MESSAGE toward the top */

        const content = section.querySelector(
          ".relative.z-10"
        );

        if (content) {
          content.style.justifyContent = "flex-start";
        }

      }

    } else {

      /* Restore background */

      bg1.style.opacity = "1";
      bg2.style.opacity = "0";

      /* Read More button text */

      summary.textContent = "▶ Read More";


      if (isMobile) {

        profileLeft.style.display = "";
        introductionCard.style.display = "";
        messageCard.style.width = "";

        const content = section.querySelector(
          ".relative.z-10"
        );

        if (content) {
          content.style.justifyContent = "";
        }

      }

    }

  });

});
</script>

</Layout>
